{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1c9ea3c5-87b7-461e-9caf-e82d18dc2677","agentId":"a2392aaec64306cb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient: read only what you need; 5 checks; one 400px screenshot; report under 100 words. Do not edit app.py (report include lines), mes-log-mcp/mes/* except NEW mes/jobs.py, nor any systems_*/electrical_*/layout_* file. Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; cuore FastAPI + Jinja, phone-first (classes at the end of cuore/web/static/cuore.css); Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe; tests use a temp CUORE_STATE_DIR. Read docs/research/review-2026-09-14/mes_binary_analysis.md and docs/research/MES_INTEGRATION_SURFACE.md briefly for how MultiEcuScan structures a session (vehicle -> module -> errors / parameters / actuators / adjustments / info -> scan report).\n\nGoal: cuore as a mechanic's technical tool: one Job (case) per visit that aligns driver input, mechanic input, test results and malfunctions into one logical flow.\n1. mes-log-mcp/mes/jobs.py: JSONL store <state>/jobs.jsonl: {id, vin, opened_at, closed_at, technician, complaint (driver's words), status: open|verifying|closed, outcome: fixed|not_fixed|deferred|None, hypotheses: [{id, text, system, status: open|supported|refuted|confirmed, evidence_for: [ref], evidence_against: [ref], next_test: str}], actions: [{at, kind: test|inspection|repair|part|clear|note, text, ref}], verification: {readiness_at, codes_returned: [], verdict}, links: {symptom_ids, note_ids, media_ids, feedback_ids, service_record_ids, inspection_ids}}. A ref = {\"kind\": \"code\"|\"freeze_frame\"|\"actuator\"|\"live\"|\"inspection\"|\"symptom\"|\"note\"|\"media\"|\"dealer\"|\"bulletin\", \"id\", \"label\"}. Functions open/close/add_hypothesis/set_hypothesis/add_action/attach/load/current(vin). MCP tools job_open/job_current/job_add_action/job_set_hypothesis in mes-log-mcp/server.py.\n2. cuore/services/jobs_bridge.py: build_job_view(vin, job_id=None) assembling the current job with auto-gathered evidence from existing bridges: dossier verdict and open-work steps (dossier_bridge.build_view), symptoms (timeline_bridge), notes, media counts, feedback open count, dealer results, electrical inspections (electrical_bridge if present), systems correlation chains (systems_bridge if present) -> suggested hypotheses (e.g. \"EVAP: ESIM signal path\" and \"EVAP: ECM calibration\" from the fault tree/bulletins, each pre-filled with evidence_for/against drawn from real data: smoke tests, actuator results, freeze-frame fuel flags, clear history). Never invent evidence: each ref must point at a real record.\n3. cuore/api/jobs.py (CRUD JSON) and cuore/web/jobs_routes.py: /v/{vin}/job page (Job tab; add it to _vbar.html after Dossier): header (complaint, technician, opened, status), a stepper of the MES-like flow: 1 Complaint & symptoms (driver input) -> 2 Scan & codes -> 3 Tests & inspections -> 4 Hypotheses (ledger: each with evidence for/against as chips linking to the source, status buttons 44px, next test) -> 5 Repair actions -> 6 Verify (readiness link, codes returned) -> 7 Outcome & handover (link to /v/{vin}/report.pdf). Plain forms (no-JS) to add/edit each part; auto-gathered evidence shown with its date and source. Close job -> outcome required.\n4. Tests (5): open job via form; suggested hypotheses include an EVAP one with >=1 real evidence_for ref; add action and set hypothesis status round trip; close with outcome; page 200 at 400px with no overflow (CDP pattern; cleanup via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py). Run + check_api.py."},"uuid":"473a5a81-448c-4d7b-b143-306a7d3c10ba","timestamp":"2026-10-08T03:03:29.517Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
