{"parentUuid":"fd16ee1e-5e82-4742-a69a-8ec8d025a1ae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3ace81fc-54d9-4a04-be82-e269831a6f4d","agentId":"a2392aaec64306cb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vt8BbZL7yDYvqs9ox9bgGv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Checks for the \"Codes vs. what the driver notices\" timeline page\n2\t(``/v/{vin}/timeline``) and the symptom form it shares with ``code.html``.\n3\t\n4\tSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_live_dashboard_page.py`` (this file's\n5\tscreenshot/CDP plumbing is copied from there almost verbatim): ``\n6\tCUORE_STATE_DIR`` is pointed at a throwaway directory BEFORE cuore is\n7\timported, and ``cuore/web/timeline_routes.py`` is not yet wired into\n8\t``cuore/app.py``, so ``_app_with_router()``/the server snippet include it\n9\tthemselves if ``create_app()`` did not already pick it up.\n10\t\n11\t``cuore/services/timeline_bridge.py`` is being built in parallel by another\n12\tagent and may not exist yet -- ``timeline_routes`` falls back to its own\n13\tbuilt-in fixture in that case (see that module's docstring), so every check\n14\tbelow runs either way. The one check that is genuinely bridge-dependent\n15\t(the symptom actually appearing back on the page after a POST, since the\n16\tfixture path has nowhere durable to write it) is skipped with a clear note\n17\twhen the bridge is absent, per the task brief.\n18\t\n19\tParts:\n20\t  1. The page, the symptom form and the code page's feel card, over\n21\t     TestClient.\n22\t  2. Visual grammar content checks on the rendered SVG: every legend line\n23\t     style (solid/dashed/dotted/thick) and marker shape, the fuel band, and\n24\t     that dashed/dotted strokes are actually emitted.\n25\t  3. A real server, screenshotted at 400px and 1400px over CDP, with a\n26\t     horizontal-overflow check (the page itself must never scroll sideways\n27\t     -- only the chart's own box may).\n28\t\n29\tRun:\n30\t    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_timeline_page.py\n31\t\"\"\"\n32\t\n33\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n34\t\n35\timport base64\n36\timport itertools\n37\timport json\n38\timport os\n39\timport socket\n40\timport subprocess\n41\timport sys\n42\timport tempfile\n43\timport time\n44\timport urllib.request\n45\tfrom pathlib import Path\n46\t\n47\tos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-timeline-\")\n48\tos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n49\t\n50\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n51\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n52\t\n53\tfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient  # noqa: E402\n54\t\n55\tfrom cuore.app import create_app  # noqa: E402\n56\tfrom cuore.web import timeline_routes  # noqa: E402\n57\t\n58\tfrom websockets.sync.client import connect  # noqa: E402\n59\t\n60\tVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"           # the Stelvio -- real corpus\n61\tEDGE_CANDIDATES = [\n62\t    r\"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe\",\n63\t    r\"C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe\",\n64\t]\n65\tSCRATCHPAD = Path(r\"C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\"\n66\t                  r\"\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\")\n67\t\n68\tBRIDGE_PRESENT = timeline_routes._bridge() is not None\n69\t\n70\tfailures: list[str] = []"}]},"uuid":"ea397365-9de0-4c92-8e89-90c7577020da","timestamp":"2026-10-08T03:13:18.070Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_timeline_page.py","content":"\"\"\"Checks for the \"Codes vs. what the driver notices\" timeline page\n(``/v/{vin}/timeline``) and the symptom form it shares with ``code.html``.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_live_dashboard_page.py`` (this file's\nscreenshot/CDP plumbing is copied from there almost verbatim): ``\nCUORE_STATE_DIR`` is pointed at a throwaway directory BEFORE cuore is\nimported, and ``cuore/web/timeline_routes.py`` is not yet wired into\n``cuore/app.py``, so ``_app_with_router()``/the server snippet include it\nthemselves if ``create_app()`` did not already pick it up.\n\n``cuore/services/timeline_bridge.py`` is being built in parallel by another\nagent and may not exist yet -- ``timeline_routes`` falls back to its own\nbuilt-in fixture in that case (see that module's docstring), so every check\nbelow runs either way. The one check that is genuinely bridge-dependent\n(the symptom actually appearing back on the page after a POST, since the\nfixture path has nowhere durable to write it) is skipped with a clear note\nwhen the bridge is absent, per the task brief.\n\nParts:\n  1. The page, the symptom form and the code page's feel card, over\n     TestClient.\n  2. Visual grammar content checks on the rendered SVG: every legend line\n     style (solid/dashed/dotted/thick) and marker shape, the fuel band, and\n     that dashed/dotted strokes are actually emitted.\n  3. A real server, screenshotted at 400px and 1400px over CDP, with a\n     horizontal-overflow check (the page itself must never scroll sideways\n     -- only the chart's own box may).\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_timeline_page.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport base64\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport os\nimport socket\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nimport urllib.request\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-timeline-\")\nos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom cuore.app import create_app  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.web import timeline_routes  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom websockets.sync.client import connect  # noqa: E402\n\nVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"           # the Stelvio -- real corpus\nEDGE_CANDIDATES = [\n    r\"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe\",\n    r\"C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft\\Edge\\Application\\msedge.exe\",\n]\nSCRATCHPAD = Path(r\"C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\"\n                  r\"\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\")\n\nBRIDGE_PRESENT = timeline_routes._bridge() is not None\n\nfailures: list[str] = []","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":402}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd16ee1e-5e82-4742-a69a-8ec8d025a1ae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
